    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3616" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărĭdaeus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀριδαῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a natural son of Philip
				of Macedon by the dancer Philinna</i>, <i>brother
				and successor of Alexander the Great</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 9,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 15
			al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 10, 17</span></i>.—Also called
			Philippus, <i><span class="en">Nep. Phoc. 3, 3</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Just. 13,
			3</span></i>.</div>
